---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CTA from '~/components/CTA.astro';

// DRAFT — noindex until Dennis confirms the items flagged below, then
// remove `noindex` and add /security to the footer.
//
// CLAIMS VERIFIED against public/api/advisor.php (2026-05-29):
//   - anthropic-zdr: true on every API request (line ~210)
//   - no database, no content logging (only error text + hashed-IP rate counter)
//   - drop-doc upload read for text extraction, not persisted by KKT
//   - calculator inputs stay client-side (CalculatorPreview.tsx)
// TO CONFIRM before publish (do NOT assert without Dennis):
//   - formal certifications (ISO 27001 / SOC 2) — currently NOT claimed
//   - named DPO / formal DPA / sub-processor list
//   - business-correspondence retention period
//   - confirm no analytics/tracking is added later
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Security & privacy — KKT"
  description="How KKT handles your data: the advisor, dropped documents, the calculator, and our GDPR posture as an EU firm."
  noindex={true}
>
  <article class="prose-page">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-label">Security &amp; privacy</div>
      <h1 class="h1-page">How we handle your data.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        We ask senior people to share real, sensitive material — a P&amp;L,
        a KPI dashboard, an operating situation. That only works if the
        data handling is honest and plain. Here is exactly what happens to
        what you share, in the same language we use everywhere else.
      </p>

      <section data-reveal class="sec">
        <div class="section-label">The advisor &amp; dropped documents</div>
        <h2 class="h2-section">Private by default. Not stored.</h2>
        <p>
          When you ask the advisor a question, or drop a document for it to
          audit, the content is processed in real time to generate the
          answer and then it is gone. There is no account, no database, and
          no log of what you typed or uploaded.
        </p>
        <ul class="points" data-reveal-stagger>
          <li>
            <strong>Zero data retention at the AI layer.</strong> Requests
            to our AI provider (Anthropic&rsquo;s Claude) carry a
            zero-data-retention flag, so your inputs are not retained by the
            provider or used to train models.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>No storage on our side.</strong> We run no database and
            write no message content to disk. A dropped file is read once to
            extract its text, passed to the model, and not kept.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>No content in our logs.</strong> The only operational
            record is a rate-limit counter keyed to a one-way hash of your
            IP address with timestamps — never the message or the document.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>You choose what to share.</strong> The advisor never
            requires a document. Share only what you are comfortable
            sharing; redact first if you prefer.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <div class="callout">
          <p>
            If you would not put it in an email to us, do not put it in the
            advisor. We treat both with the same care &mdash; but plain
            honesty beats a false promise.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section data-reveal class="sec">
        <div class="section-label">The Cost of Doing Nothing calculator</div>
        <h2 class="h2-section">Your numbers stay in your browser.</h2>
        <p>
          The calculator runs entirely on your device. The figures you
          enter are not sent to us &mdash; there is no submission step that
          transmits them &mdash; unless you explicitly choose to attach your
          results when booking a diagnostic. That is stated in the tool
          itself, and it is the whole point: it should be useful to a CFO
          who does not want their numbers leaving their machine.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-reveal class="sec">
        <div class="section-label">Where we are, which law applies</div>
        <h2 class="h2-section">An EU firm, under GDPR.</h2>
        <p>
          KKT is Kitty Kat Technologies O&Uuml; , registered at J&otilde;e 7,
          10151 Tallinn, Estonia. As an EU entity we operate under the
          General Data Protection Regulation. Any personal data you send us
          directly &mdash; an email, a contact-form message &mdash; is used
          only to respond to you and to run the engagement, never sold and
          never shared beyond what a specific engagement requires.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section data-reveal class="sec">
        <div class="section-label">What we do not do</div>
        <h2 class="h2-section">The short list.</h2>
        <ul class="points" data-reveal-stagger>
          <li>We do not sell or rent your data to anyone.</li>
          <li>We do not use what you share with the advisor to train models.</li>
          <li>We do not run advertising or cross-site tracking on this site.</li>
          <li>We do not require an account to use anything here.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section data-reveal class="sec">
        <div class="section-label">Procurement &amp; due diligence</div>
        <h2 class="h2-section">Need more for a review?</h2>
        <p>
          If your procurement or security team needs a data-processing
          agreement, a sub-processor list, or answers to a vendor-security
          questionnaire before an engagement, write to us and we will work
          through it directly. We would rather have that conversation early
          than paper over it.
        </p>
        <p class="meta-line">
          Data &amp; privacy questions:
          <a href="mailto:hello@kittykat.tech">hello@kittykat.tech</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <CTA
      heading="Questions before you share anything?"
      body="Ask first. We would rather answer a data-handling question up front than have you wonder about it later."
      primaryLabel="Email hello@kittykat.tech"
      primaryHref="mailto:hello@kittykat.tech"
      secondaryLabel="How we work"
      secondaryHref="/approach"
    />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose-page {
    padding-top: clamp(40px, 6vh, 72px);
    padding-bottom: clamp(56px, 9vh, 96px);
  }
  .section-label { margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .h1-page {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4.5vw, 48px);
    line-height: 1.16;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    max-width: 22ch;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: clamp(17px, 2vw, 20px);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .sec {
    margin-top: clamp(40px, 6vh, 64px);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 36px;
  }
  .sec .section-label { margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .sec h2 { margin-bottom: 16px; max-width: 26ch; }
  .sec p { max-width: 64ch; margin-bottom: 14px; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .points {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    max-width: 720px;
  }
  .points li {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .points strong { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .callout {
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    padding: 18px 22px;
    background: var(--surface-alt);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;
    max-width: 720px;
  }
  .callout p {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: clamp(17px, 2.2vw, 20px);
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 44ch;
  }
  .meta-line {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text-muted) !important;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  .meta-line a { color: var(--text-primary); font-weight: 500; }
</style>
